  "answer": "This looks like a known problem. I found no ticket that mentions \"Open url in Edge\" itself, so the match is based on how it behaves. PowerToys#46587 describes the same symptom for fallback commands. \"Open url in Edge\" is a fallback result generated from the text you type. Pin to Dock is offered on it and the item is marked as pinned, but nothing appears on the Dock. In that ticket a maintainer said fallbacks arguably shouldn't be pinnable at all, and that improvements for pinning them are in progress. PowerToys#48254 is a related case where an item is flagged as pinned but never shows on the Dock. I found no fix or workaround for fallbacks in the archive. You could pin a real command or app instead. For example, create a shortcut (.lnk) or a Command Palette bookmark for the msteams:// link and pin that. Also, try unpinning the invisible entry, then update PowerToys to see if a later build fixes it."
 },
